# TurboRisk developer guide

TurboRisk is a Lazarus/Free Pascal port of Mario Ferrari's Risk-style strategy
game. The repository also contains TRSim and its command-line runner, TRComp
(the TRP editor/compiler/routine tester), and TRMap (the map editor). The
project port is complete; this is not a pending Delphi-to-Lazarus conversion.

## Build

Install Lazarus and Free Pascal, then build the projects from the repository
root. On Windows, for example:

```powershell
C:\lazarus\lazbuild.exe .\TurboRisk.lpi
C:\lazarus\lazbuild.exe .\TRSim.lpi
C:\lazarus\lazbuild.exe .\TRSimCLI.lpi
C:\lazarus\lazbuild.exe .\TRComp.lpi
C:\lazarus\lazbuild.exe .\TRMap.lpi
```

TRMap's SVG import/export requires Lazarus `fpvectorial`. Build `lhelp` with
`C:\lazarus\lazbuild.exe .\lhelp\lhelp.lpi` when a platform needs the separate
Lazarus help viewer. The Windows CHM source is in `Doc\HelpSource`; after editing it, rebuild
the tracked `Doc\TurboRisk.chm` from the repository root with
`chmcmd .\Doc\HelpSource\TurboRisk.hhp`.

## Regression checks

```powershell
C:\lazarus\lazbuild.exe .\tests\TRCompWorkflowTests.lpi
.\tests\TRCompWorkflowTests.exe
C:\lazarus\lazbuild.exe .\tests\TRMapWorkflowTests.lpi
.\tests\TRMapWorkflowTests.exe
.\tests\Run-TRSimCLITests.ps1
```

The workflows cover TRComp routine validation/execution-context restoration,
TRMap import/edit/save/validation, and TRSimCLI scheduling, deterministic runs,
logging, and bot smoke tests. `TRComp.md`, `TRMap.md`, and `TRSimCLI.md` contain
current tool-specific usage and feature details.

## Current scope and known issue

Custom maps use a fixed 42-territory, six-continent topology. TRMap edits map
artwork and territory points; it does not change the game's territory-border
rules. It imports SVG and BMP artwork, with limitations documented in
`TRMap.md` and the map-editor help.

TurboRisk's old online news/update service was removed during the Lazarus port.
The historical preference and help pages may still mention it; they do not
describe a current feature.

[Issue #28](https://github.com/brian-scott-andrews/TurboRisk/issues/28) remains
open. It tracks an intermittent TRP Placement access violation reported under
specific game/configuration conditions. The historical report below is not
evidence that the problem currently reproduces on every platform or with every
named bot; consult the issue and current regression tests for verified status.

## Historical developer notes

The following notes are retained from the original 2019-era port/developer
README. They describe historical context and proposals, not the current
implementation status.

The Lazarus/Free Pascal port was tested at the time on Linux Mint 18 and
Windows 7. The Windows Help format replaced Delphi's original help system; the
repository includes the `lhelp` viewer. PascalScript is built with
`PS_DELPHIDIV` because TRP scripts rely on Delphi-style integer division.

The original port notes described a Linux `TCanvas.FloodFill` workaround and
reported an intermittent access violation for some TRPs under particular
conditions. The current state of that issue is tracked in [#28](https://github.com/brian-scott-andrews/TurboRisk/issues/28);
do not use that old report alone as a current compatibility guarantee.

### Original author notes

The notes below are from Mario Ferrari's original developer README:

- `Supervisor` in `Globals.pas` manages game turns and phases. Its handoff
  between the main-window event manager and the game supervisor is
  intentionally non-obvious.
- The source consists of many units; the original author considered it
  structured and commented.
- The original map-format discussion predates TRMap's current SVG/BMP import
  and export workflows.

The original wishlist mentioned completing comment/identifier translation,
vector maps, and multiplayer. These were proposals at the time they were
written, not a statement of current work in progress.
